  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0e821502",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What does the table above tell us?\n",
    "Although the mean duration does not accually tell us the minimum possible duration between two stations, it provides a useful indication of what a typical trip looks like. \n",
    "\n",
    "The table shows station pairs with hundres and thousands of bike-trips, where the average duration is several minutes, yet the shortest recorded time is only one second. This strongly suggest that some values are incorrect or unrealistic. \n",
    "\n",
    "On another note this does make me question the dataset and its accuracy. Are these simply a small number of isolated data quality issues, or could they indicate more problems with the data?\n",
    "\n",
    "For now let's atleast flag trips with a duration smaller than one second. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "244531ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Flag trips that are under 1 second\n",
    "trips_silver = trips_silver.withColumn(\n",
    "    \"short_trip_flag\",\n",
    "    when(col(\"duration\") < 60, True).otherwise(False)\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
