  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b919751f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Could a city bike realistically be used for appocimately 22 hours?\n",
    "\n",
    "Accoring to Oslo Bysykkel, a fully charged electric bike has an estimate range of around 70 kilometers. The battery does not necessarily limit the recorded trip duration, as the bike can remain parked while the rental is still active and you can manually ride the bike if the battery runs out. \n",
    "\n",
    "If the dataset included distance travelled we could better investigate whether the bicycle was actively used.\n",
    "\n",
    "Possible explainations for the long duration\n",
    "- The user forgot to return the bike or didn't properly complete the return process.\n",
    "- The bike was parked for several hours while the rental was still active. \n",
    "- The recorded timestamp contains an error. \n",
    "- Maybe others?"
   ]
  },
